# Team Knowledge Base Q&A System

Upload your team's internal documents (PDF/TXT) and ask natural language questions. The system retrieves relevant chunks and uses an LLM (Groq) to generate accurate, grounded answers.

## Features
- Upload multiple PDF/TXT documents
- Ask questions in plain English
- Answers are based **only** on your documents, no hallucinations
- Shows which source documents were used
- Full containerized stack (Docker Compose)
- Free to use locally or deploy to cloud

## Quick Start (Local)
1. Clone the repo
2. Create a `.env` file from `.env` and add your [Groq API key](https://console.groq.com)
3. Run `docker-compose up --build`
4. Open http://localhost:8501 in your browser

## Deployment
- Backend: can be deployed to Render, Fly.io, or AWS
- Frontend: can be deployed to Streamlit Community Cloud or Hugging Face Spaces
- See `doc.md` for detailed architecture and learning guide

## Tech Stack
- Backend: FastAPI + ChromaDB + SentenceTransformers + Groq
- Frontend: Streamlit
- Deployment: Docker + GitHub Actions (CI)